{"id": "unknown-2026-11-01-005", "date": "2026-11-01", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 44, "weekday": "Sun"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India extends cotton duty exemption until Dec 31; SIMA welcomes move", "content": "India has extended the cotton import duty exemption until December 31, 2026, amid a projected supply shortage. \nSIMA welcomed the move, saying it would help textile manufacturers secure raw materials and meet export commitments. \nThe association urged the government to extend the exemption until 2030 to ensure supply and price stability.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-extends-cotton-duty-exemption-until-dec-31-sima-welcomes-move-314695-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
